        "question": "How do you handle GDPR for a US startup?",
        "answer": "GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation) applies to any organisation that processes personal data of EU residents regardless of where the organisation is located. A US startup with EU users is subject to GDPR. Key GDPR requirements for startups: lawful basis for processing (typically legitimate interests for B2B products, or consent for B2C products document the lawful basis for each data processing activity), data subject rights (right to access, right to erasure (right to be forgotten), right to data portability these must be technically implementable, not just stated in the privacy policy), data processing agreements (sign a DPA with every vendor that processes EU personal data on your behalf AWS, Stripe, Resend, Intercom all provide GDPR DPAs), and data breach notification (notify the relevant supervisory authority within 72 hours of becoming aware of a breach affecting EU residents). ClickMasters implements the technical components of GDPR compliance (data deletion workflows, data export, consent management) as part of every startup engagement."
