        "body": "The modern data stack from a CTO's perspective: ELT over ETL (extract and load raw data to the warehouse first (Airbyte, Fivetran), then transform in the warehouse using dbt this approach keeps the raw data available for re-transformation as requirements change, rather than the traditional ETL model where data is transformed before loading and changes require re-extracting from source), dbt (data build tool the SQL transformation layer that introduces software engineering practices to data work: version control, testing (dbt test), documentation, and modular reusable models ClickMasters implements dbt as the standard transformation tool for all data warehouse engagements), and data quality (Great Expectations or dbt tests automated data quality checks on every pipeline run, alerts when data quality drops below acceptable thresholds the data reliability layer that prevents silent data quality failures from corrupting analytics)."
