        "title": "Database Selection Framework for CTOs",
        "body": "The CTO's database selection framework: start with PostgreSQL (PostgreSQL handles 95% of production workloads correctly relational data, JSON documents (JSONB), full-text search, geospatial queries (PostGIS), time series (TimescaleDB extension), and graph queries (recursive CTEs) before considering specialised databases, confirm that PostgreSQL cannot handle the workload), add Redis when needed (Redis for caching (read-heavy data that is expensive to compute), session storage (stateless application servers), rate limiting (atomic increment operations), and pub/sub messaging not as a primary database), and introduce specialised databases only when genuinely necessary (Elasticsearch for full-text search at scale (1M+ documents with complex relevance requirements), InfluxDB/Timescale for high-frequency time series (IoT telemetry, financial tick data), Cassandra for high-write distributed data with no complex queries)."
