        "question": "How do you set up CI/CD for a startup that does not have a DevOps engineer?",
        "answer": "Startup CI/CD with GitHub Actions and no dedicated DevOps engineer: create a .github/workflows/ci.yml file that runs on every pull request (install dependencies, run the test suite, run ESLint, run TypeScript type checking fail the PR if any check fails), create a .github/workflows/deploy.yml that runs on merge to main (build the Docker image, push to ECR (or use Vercel's automatic deployment), update the ECS service or trigger a Vercel deployment). The entire CI/CD setup for a Next.js application on Vercel: a single GitHub Actions workflow file, the Vercel GitHub integration (which handles deployment automatically), and a branch protection rule in GitHub that requires CI checks to pass before merge. Total engineering time: 1-2 days. ClickMasters sets up CI/CD as a standard component of every startup engagement not as an optional add-on."
