        "title": "IoT Security Architecture for CTOs",
        "body": "IoT security concerns for CTOs: device identity (each device must have a unique cryptographic identity (X.509 certificate or JWT with device-specific private key) shared secrets across a device fleet are a catastrophic security failure (compromising one device compromises all), mutual TLS (device authenticates to the server and server authenticates to the device prevents both unauthorized devices from connecting and prevents devices from connecting to malicious servers), certificate rotation (device certificates have finite lifetimes the OTA mechanism must support certificate rotation before expiry, without requiring physical device access), and secure boot (verify the firmware signature before executing prevent a compromised device from running attacker-controlled firmware even if physical access is achieved)."
