        "answer": "Pre-launch load testing for startup founders: define the expected traffic (use the press release reach estimate a TechCrunch post generates 10,000-50,000 unique visitors in 24 hours, of which 1-5% may sign up model the concurrent user count based on these estimates), write a k6 load test script (k6 is a JavaScript-based load testing tool write a test that simulates 1,000 concurrent users signing up, browsing, and completing the core workflow 2-4 hours of engineering time), run the test against a staging environment (run the k6 test at 10x expected peak traffic identify the first component that fails under load: the database, the API server, or an external dependency), and fix the bottlenecks (add caching for the most expensive database queries, increase the connection pool size, add auto-scaling if not already configured). Total effort: 1-2 days for a startup with a simple MVP. ClickMasters runs pre-launch load tests as a standard component of every startup MVP engagement."
