        "question": "What is the process for resolving technical disagreements between ClickMasters and the CTO?",
        "answer": "Technical disagreements between ClickMasters and the CTO are resolved through a structured process: ClickMasters presents the disagreement explicitly (rather than silently implementing the approach the CTO prefers while disagreeing internally), documents the two positions (what ClickMasters recommends and why, what the CTO prefers and why), identifies the decision criteria (what technical factors determine which approach is better performance, maintainability, security, cost, time to implement), and defers to the CTO (the CTO has the authority to make the final technical decision and ClickMasters implements it without passive resistance). The ADR documents the final decision, including the alternative that was not chosen, so the context is available if the decision needs to be revisited. The goal is technical honesty, not technical agreement ClickMasters tells CTOs what we think, even when it is not what they want to hear, and then implements whatever the CTO decides."
