        "answer": "Minimum viable design for a startup MVP: one consistent font (Inter or Geist free, excellent rendering on screens, appropriate for both headings and body text do not spend time on custom typography at MVP stage), a colour palette of four colours (primary (your brand colour), primary-dark (darker variant for hover states), neutral (grey for backgrounds, borders, secondary text), and semantic colours (green for success, red for error, amber for warning use Tailwind's built-in colour system to avoid designing a palette from scratch)), a spacing scale (use Tailwind's default spacing scale (4px base unit) consistently do not introduce custom spacing values), and accessible contrast ratios (use Tailwind's text-gray-900 on white backgrounds, ensure all interactive elements have 4.5:1 contrast ratio prevents ADA accessibility lawsuits). This minimal design language takes 1 day to define and enables engineers to build consistent UIs without making individual design decisions."
