        "body": "The architectural choices that determine whether a SaaS product is pleasant or painful for an engineering team to operate: PostgreSQL Row-Level Security for multi-tenancy (database-enforced tenant isolation that cannot be accidentally bypassed by application code the safest multi-tenancy pattern for a small team), feature flags from day one (LaunchDarkly or Growthbook deploy code independently of releasing features, run A/B tests, gradually roll out to a percentage of customers the practice that separates high-performing engineering teams from low-performing ones), and event-driven architecture where appropriate (Kafka or SQS for operations that do not need to be synchronous email sending, webhook delivery, analytics processing improve API response times and isolate failures)."
