        "question": "What security does a startup need before raising Series A?",
        "answer": "Series A investors and their portfolio company enterprise customers will scrutinise the startup's security posture more than at seed stage. Security baseline for Series A readiness: SOC 2 Type II in progress or completed (start the observation period at least 6 months before the target Series A date), penetration test completed (a clean or remediated pen test report demonstrates security programme maturity), GDPR/CCPA compliance documentation (privacy policy, data processing agreements with key vendors, consent management), no known critical CVEs in production dependencies (automated dependency scanning with a remediation process for critical findings), and incident response plan (a documented procedure for responding to a data breach required for SOC 2, expected by enterprise customers, and legally required in most jurisdictions). ClickMasters prepares startup Series A security packages covering all five requirements."
