        "question": "What infrastructure metrics should a PM track?",
        "answer": "Infrastructure metrics for PMs (expressed in product terms): uptime percentage and incidents (the PM should know the product's actual uptime over the last 90 days and the root cause of each incident this data informs the SLA the PM can commit to in customer contracts and the investment case for reliability improvements), deployment frequency (the number of production deployments per week is the best proxy for development velocity a low deployment frequency (less than weekly) indicates CI/CD friction or an excessively large release cycle that is slowing feature delivery), and error rate (the percentage of API requests that return an error a rising error rate in the PM's analytics dashboard indicates a product quality problem before it becomes a customer complaint). ClickMasters provides the PM with a weekly infrastructure summary covering these three metrics, in plain English rather than technical terminology."
