        "answer": "Database migrations (changes to the database schema) are one of the highest-risk activities in a running production product they can cause downtime, data loss, or performance degradation if not executed correctly. What the PM needs to know: zero-downtime migrations require engineering investment (the expand-contract pattern: add the new structure alongside the old, migrate data in batches, switch the application to the new structure, drop the old a 3-step process that takes longer than a single migration but has no user-visible impact), migrations should be planned in advance of the sprint they are needed (database migrations that are not tested in staging before production deployment cause incidents ClickMasters includes migration testing in the sprint's QA checklist), and migrations are a deployment risk factor (the PM should be notified when a sprint includes a significant database migration this is the sprint where a staged rollout (feature flags, canary deployment) reduces the risk of a migration-related incident reaching all users simultaneously). ClickMasters communicates migration risk to the PM as part of sprint planning."
