        "title": "API Design for CTOs",
        "body": "API design decisions that a CTO will live with: REST vs GraphQL vs gRPC (REST for most external APIs (wide client support, simple caching, well-understood), GraphQL for product APIs with diverse client requirements (avoids over-fetching/under-fetching, enables frontend teams to iterate without backend changes), gRPC for internal service-to-service communication (binary protocol, strongly typed, efficient at high throughput)), API versioning strategy (URI versioning (/v1/, /v2/) is simple and explicit; header versioning is cleaner but harder to test; no versioning is only appropriate for private APIs with a single client), and API gateway (AWS API Gateway or Kong rate limiting, authentication, request routing, and observability for APIs that are exposed to the internet the correct separation point between public API concerns and business logic)."
