        "question": "How do you design a startup product for mobile when the budget is limited?",
        "answer": "Mobile-first responsive design is the correct approach for startup products targeting consumers or SMB users who may access the product from mobile. The design process: design the mobile layout first (the smaller screen forces prioritisation if a feature does not fit on mobile, it is not important enough to be above the fold), then expand to desktop (adding features and detail as the screen size increases). Tailwind CSS with responsive prefixes (sm:, md:, lg:) makes responsive design efficient to implement most ClickMasters MVP designs are fully responsive with no additional engineering effort because the design is built mobile-first. The exception: complex data-heavy interfaces (financial dashboards, admin interfaces with large tables, CAD or design tools) these should be desktop-first with a simplified mobile view rather than attempting full parity across screen sizes."
