        "answer": "The decision framework: hire a designer (full-time or fractional) if design is a core competitive differentiator of the product (consumer app where the UX is the product, brand-driven consumer goods, fashion, home décor industries where aesthetics are a primary purchase driver). Use a design agency or ClickMasters at MVP stage if design is important but not the primary differentiator (most B2B SaaS, developer tools, marketplace products the product's value is in the workflow, the data, or the network, and design is a quality threshold, not the moat). The correct MVP design investment is functional and conversion-optimised it does not need to win a design award, it needs to get users to the core value quickly and convert trials to paid customers. ClickMasters delivers this standard at MVP budget levels, typically $5,000-$15,000 for a complete MVP design."
